Causal/Nonanticipatory System
A system whose current output depends on past and current inputs but not on future inputs.
• A noncausal system can predict or anticipate future inputs.
• Causality is an intrinsic property of a physical system.
• Causality: A necessary condition for a system to be built or implemented in the real world.
• For causal systems,
